-- title:
--   Generic Atkin–Lehner θ as base change of rational σ
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $p$ and a nonzero modulus $M$ with $p \mid M$ and $p^2 \nmid M$, and a subgroup $H \le (\mathbb{Z}/M)^\times$ containing the kernel of the reduction $(\mathbb{Z}/M)^\times \to (\mathbb{Z}/(M/p))^\times$ (stated as: every unit mapping to $1$ under `ZMod.unitsMap` for $M/p \mid M$ lies in $H$). Write $\bar{\mathbb{Q}}$ for `AlgebraicClosure ℚ`, let `coeffEmb` be the coefficientwise ring map $\mathrm{Laurent}(\mathbb{Q}) \to \mathrm{Laurent}(\bar{\mathbb{Q}})$, let `xHFunctionFieldBar M H` be the $\bar{\mathbb{Q}}$-subfield of $\mathrm{Laurent}(\bar{\mathbb{Q}})$ generated by the `coeffEmb`-image of `xHFunctionField M H`, and let `qExpand R p` be the substitution $\sum a_n q^n \mapsto \sum a_n q^{pn}$. Two data are given: a $\bar{\mathbb{Q}}$-algebra automorphism $\theta$ of `xHFunctionFieldBar M H` such that whenever an element $f$ of that field has the same underlying Laurent series as an element $u$ of `xHFunctionFieldBar (M / p) (infSubgroup p M H hpM)` — the base-changed field at level $M/p$ for the image of $H$ — the series of $\theta f$ is `qExpand` at $p$ of that of $u$; and a $\mathbb{Q}$-algebra automorphism $\sigma$ of `qExpFunctionFieldC ℚ (ΓM M H)`, the subfield of $\mathrm{Laurent}(\mathbb{Q})$ generated over $\mathbb{Q}$ by ratios of integral $q$-expansions of modular forms of equal weight for `ΓM M H`, obeying the same law relative to `qExpFunctionFieldC ℚ (ΓN p M H hpM)`. The conclusion is that for every $f$ in `qExpFunctionFieldC ℚ (ΓM M H)` the Laurent series of $\theta$ applied to `coeffEmb` of $f$ equals `coeffEmb` of the Laurent series of $\sigma f$; in particular the membership proof for $f$ serves to place `coeffEmb` of $f$ in the base-changed field.
--
--   This is the descent statement for the generic Atkin–Lehner-type automorphism: a $\bar{\mathbb{Q}}$-automorphism characterised by the degeneracy law $q \mapsto q^p$ at level $M/p$ is the base change of any rational automorphism with the same law, the trivial deck group of the covering of modular curves forcing uniqueness. It feeds the construction of prolongation data for place specialisation on $X_H$ and the computation of the action of such automorphisms on modular unit $q$-expansions.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_XHDRLevel_algEquiv_coeffEmb_eq_coeffEmb_ratAlgEquiv_of_atkinLehner_generic.lean

